.TH "MEDIASTREAM.REMOVETRACK_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
MediaStream.removetrack_event \- MediaStream: removetrack event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]removetrack\f[B]\f[R] event is fired when a new
\f[CR]MediaStreamTrack\f[R] object has been removed from a
\f[CR]MediaStream\f[R].
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqremovetrack\(dq, (event) => { })

onremovetrack = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]MediaStreamTrackEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
Using \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] stream = \f[B]new\f[R] MediaStream();

stream.addEventListener(\(dqremovetrack\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(ga${event.track.kind} track removed\(ga);
});
.EE
.PP
Using the \f[CR]onremovetrack\f[R] event handler property:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] stream = \f[B]new\f[R] MediaStream();

stream.onremovetrack = (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(ga${event.track.kind} track removed\(ga);
};
.EE
